# Build context for services/api/Dockerfile and services/actors/Dockerfile (E3b).
# Both are built with the repo root as context — `docker build -f services/api/Dockerfile .`
# — because the `workspace:*` protocol needs the root package.json (which is
# where the workspace globs live under bun) and the packages/* dependency
# closure visible at build time. Without this file that
# context includes every already-installed node_modules in the repo (100s of MB
# per project) plus .git, secrets, and the legacy Nhost stack.
#
# Keep in sync by hand: there is no automated check that a new top-level
# directory gets added here.

**/node_modules
**/.turbo
**/dist
**/.next
.git

# Legacy Nhost stack — D9 removes it after cutover; irrelevant to services/api and
# services/actors either way, and functions/ is a separate pnpm 10 context that
# the bun migration deliberately left alone.
nhost
functions

# The Next.js frontend and the browser suite. Neither ships in a backend
# image, and services/client's dependency tree is by far the largest in the
# repo — but their **manifests** must stay in the context. With one root
# lockfile, `--frozen-lockfile` compares that lockfile against every workspace
# member it can see; a member whose package.json is missing reads as drift and
# fails the install, even though neither backend depends on it. The `!` lines re-include just those two files
# (a later rule wins in .dockerignore, same as .gitignore).
services/client
!services/client/package.json
packages/e2e
!packages/e2e/package.json
# packages/analysis is the architecture scans' test-time foundation: a
# devDependency of actors, api and db that no runtime stage copies and a
# `--production` install never links. Same treatment as e2e — sources out,
# manifest in, for the --frozen-lockfile reason above.
packages/analysis
!packages/analysis/package.json
scripts

# Secrets and local-only files. Never let these reach a build context.
.secrets
infra/.env
infra/.env.prod
infra/.env*.local
cookies.txt
*.log
.DS_Store

# Editor/tooling noise
.vscode
.claude
.mcp.json
